{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d2770af9-920d-8f78-b0c2-8acd7c2b44b3",
  "created_at": "2026-02-25T14:02:44-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rosemarie Cirelli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:58:51-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:58:55-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Denise, great, hi! Rosemarie Cirelli here. I'm on speaker, I'm in the car, so bear with me. I'm calling about a pothole, and honestly I'm kind of done with it!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:59:10-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure. Where's the pothole?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:59:13-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's at the intersection right by 89 Narragansett Avenue, in the Fifth Ward. The corner there. It has been patched three times, Denise. Three! And it keeps reopening, every time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:59:27-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three times. And is this since the storm, or has it been going on longer?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T13:59:35-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both! They patched it in December, again in January, and then once more after last weekend's nor'easter, Saturday into Sunday. And it's already crumbling again. Wonderful, right? Hold on, sorry, I'm hunting for my keys. They fell off the seat, I'm driving, I know, I know. [pause] Okay, I'll pull over in a second. Where was I?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:00:01-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The patch is already breaking up again. Do you want me to hold while you find them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:00:09-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No no, I've got them, great! Okay. So my question is, if somebody hits that thing and wrecks a tire or a rim, does the city reimburse car damage? Because I've bumped it twice and my front end is making a noise I do not love."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:00:30-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There is a claim process for vehicle damage. I can't tell you how it'll come out, but you'd file a claim with the city, and it helps to have photos and repair estimates. I can take your info and have the right office send you the form."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:00:52-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great, yes, please do that. And can you also add the street to the repair list? Not another quick patch, a real repair. Narragansett Avenue, that corner. Whatever list you've got, I want us on it!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:01:09-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll put in a request for that location and note it's been patched three times already. That history matters. The crews are slammed after the storm, so it may not be immediate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:01:24-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Of course, I get it, they're busy! But three patches in three months, that's a lot of cold patch for one hole. Just write that down!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:01:36-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Already writing it. Let me confirm the spot: 89 Narragansett Avenue, at the intersection there. Which cross street is it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:01:46-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, it's the corner right in front of 89, where the side street comes in. I'm blanking on the name, I'm sorry. [crosstalk] If you look at the spot, it's the one with the orange paint someone sprayed around it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:04-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That helps, the orange paint. I'll put that in the notes. And what's a good callback number for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:13-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0174. That's my cell."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:16-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0174. I'll have the claim form sent to you, and the request goes to the roads crew supervisor today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:26-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wonderful! Thank you, Denise, really. Honestly I'm not mad at you, I'm just mad at the hole!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Drive safe, and pull over for those keys next time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T14:02:40-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha, great, I will! Bye now!"
    }
  ],
